{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Seek a coordinated UK-wide independent inquiry into pet food safety regulation",
        "additional_details": "Pet food is sold across UK borders, while food and feed safety responsibilities are devolved. Owners and vets should have suspected patterns of illness assessed promptly, transparently and consistently in every nation. The inquiry should examine regulators\u2019 powers, independence, evidence gathering, testing, recall thresholds, cross-border coordination and public communication, and publish its evidence, findings and recommendations for reform.",
        "background": "The UK Government should establish an independent inquiry into pet food safety regulation in England and seek agreement with the Scottish, Welsh and Northern Irish Governments for a coordinated UK-wide inquiry covering illness investigations, product testing, recalls and public communication.",
